[I] PulseAudio emulation for ALSA

[T] apulse is an alternative partial implementation of the PulseAudio API,
[T] consisting of a loader script and shared libraries with the same names
[T] as PulseAudio's. It needs no sound daemon and relies on ALSA's dmix,
[T] dsnoop and plug plugins to mix and convert multiple streams.

[U] https://github.com/i-rinat/apulse

[A] Apulse Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

